Audit 16: limit total conflict-analysis work

Since e738b54 compatible literal ends always mean a real conflict, so the
product search ran at most once per load and its 4M-state budget could not run
out. The real cost was uncharged: 10,000 rules with ~1 KiB literal ends took
8.6 s to load, and 10,000 distinct wildcard hosts took 3 s.

Decide wildcard overlap from literal ends alone and remove globs_overlap,
transition, and the state budget. Charge the bytes read for each eligible path
pair to one 4 GB budget, including comparisons that find no overlap.
ConflictAnalysisTooComplex now reports that budget running out. Identical
patterns still report a conflict before any charge. hosts_overlap no longer
allocates per pair; hosts stay uncharged because unrelated hosts must not use
budget (H6).

Test replacement: wildcard_overlap_search_refuses_to_exceed_its_budget tested
the removed globs_overlap and is replaced by
conflict_work_is_charged_for_every_eligible_comparison, which pins the exact
charge per pair in both orders and that one byte less fails closed.

The exhaustive overlap test stays and gains patterns with prefix, middle, and
suffix literals; its second assertion on the removed helper is dropped because
paths_overlap now makes that decision. Three tests are renamed because exact and
distinct-prefix pairs now do consume budget; their expectations are unchanged.

